{
  "name" : "DeBoeck2021 - Modular approach to modeling the cell cycle, simple cell cycle model",
  "description" : "<notes xmlns=\"http://www.sbml.org/sbml/level2/version4\">      <body xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">        <p>Models the production and degradation of cyclin B that drives the early embryonic cell cycle.Cyclin B is degraded by APC/C. The activity of APC/C is modeled not through biochemical interactions, but through a 'functional response curve'. This can be ultrasensitive (with the parameter alpha=0). in this case the system does not oscillate. Importantly the response can be made bistable and the form of the bistability can be easily prescribed. With a bistable response, the system oscillates.The uploaded file corresponds to the model used for Figs.3H, I in the publication.</p>      </body>    </notes>",
  "format" : {
